From 0f87ebd16664115569149ddda6de7de7d061f197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vraxa <200693817+vraxa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:05:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replay Plus 1.3: the game's own look, a real camera light
 with keys, your own controls, sharpen middle

- the panel in the game's own style: its fonts and its button and tab pictures, read from the game's data at start,
  laid out as the replay editor's own screens; on the editor's first screen it sits under the game's own title
- the camera light is a light of the game's: its renderer's spot light, placed in the world on the replay camera each
  tick, so the game lights and shadows everything with it, in the editor and in exported videos. Turning real light
  off brings back the light drawn over the picture
- light keys: on / off, power, range, beam and colour along the replay, eased between keys and switched at them, gold
  marks above the timeline, panel rows and `replayplus light ...`; R3 + dpad right puts a key that switches it when
  keyed. While a key has the light off nothing is drawn in its place
- Sharpen middle (VIDEO): an RCAS sharpen inside the lens's enlarging sample, as strong as the middle is enlarged
- overlays keep their own shape (fitted whole, never stretched, black past their edges; a picture within 13% of the
  window's shape fills it); Overlay size is a plain scale from the middle (sizes saved before are converted); WebP
  pictures are listed; the hood command takes names with spaces
- CONTROLS tab: the shortcut button (R3), each shortcut's controller button and keyboard key in columns of their own,
  and buttons or keys that load presets; one another shortcut had is swapped; the R3 helper and the menu's prompt show
  them; `replayplus bind ...`. Kept whatever look is loaded
- exports: a frame's size comes from its own buffer (the game's readback, MP4 or WebM), else that export's H.264
  setup, and nothing past it is read or written. A WebM export after an MP4 one of another picture shape, or a 2.39:1
  WebM, read and wrote past the frame and crashed the game; a 4:3 WebM was left unfinished at the bottom
- exports: focus, light and shake keys are timed from the export's start (the trim's) by the frames encoded, through
  the replay's chunks; the replay's clock stands where the editor's playhead was while a video is exported, and the
  trimmed timeline's length and playhead are the trimmed part's while the trim and the chunks are the whole replay's
- the render scale and the window shape stay as they are while a video is exported; the CPU finishing's threads are
  always joined; the video mover never throws out of its thread
